---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import NoticeBannerDemo from "../../components/NoticeBannerDemo";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Notice Banner"
  description="A full-width strip at the top of a page for something that needs action."
>
  <h1 class="docs-title">Notice Banner</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A full-width strip at the top of a page. Use it when something needs action,
    such as an integration that needs authorization. The message is on the left
    and the actions follow it.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><NoticeBannerDemo client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Notice Banner usage"
      code={`import { Button } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/button";
import { NoticeBanner } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/notice-banner";

<NoticeBanner
  aria-label="Integration authorization"
  actions={<Button variant="outline">Update permissions</Button>}
>
  <p role="status">
    <span className="font-medium text-sprout-warning">
      Google Calendar (robin@greenhouse.example) needs authorization.
    </span>{" "}
    Approve the updated permissions to continue.
  </p>
</NoticeBanner>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>NoticeBanner</code> renders a <code>section</code> with a 1px line under
      it, the surface color, and 14px muted text. <code>children</code>
      is the message. <code>actions</code> holds buttons, selects, or other controls.
      They wrap when there is no room. Leave out <code>actions</code>
      to show only the message. Other props, like <code>className</code>, go to
      the <code>section</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is one size and no variants. Below 640px the message and actions
      stack, with 8px between them, 16px side padding, and full-width actions.
      From 640px they sit on one row, centered, with 16px between them and 24px
      side padding. Long words in the message wrap.
    </p>
    <p>
      Use the default outline <code>Button</code>, 28px with 14px text, for the
      main action, next to a 32px <code>Select</code> when there is a choice. Use
      <code>size="sm"</code>, 28px with 12px text, for a single light action,
      like Dismiss. To render no banner, do not mount it.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Choosing and waiting</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Select and busy action"
      code={`<NoticeBanner
  aria-label="Integration authorization"
  actions={<>
    <div className="w-full sm:w-64">
      <Select value={selected.id} onValueChange={choose} disabled={busy}>
        <SelectTrigger width="full" aria-label="Integration to reauthorize">
          <SelectValue>{selected.name}</SelectValue>
        </SelectTrigger>
        <SelectContent>
          {items.map(item => (
            <SelectItem key={item.id} value={item.id}>{item.name}</SelectItem>
          ))}
        </SelectContent>
      </Select>
    </div>
    <Button variant="outline" disabled={busy} focusableWhenDisabled aria-busy={busy}>
      {busy ? "Please wait..." : failed ? "Check integration status" : "Update permissions"}
    </Button>
  </>}
>
  {failed
    ? <p role="alert">Authorization could not be opened. Check integration status before trying again.</p>
    : <p role="status">…</p>}
</NoticeBanner>`}
    />
    <p>
      When several items need action, put a <code>Select</code> before the button.
      Give its wrapper a full width on small screens and 16rem from 640px. While work
      runs, disable the select and button and set <code>aria-busy</code>. Add <code
        >focusableWhenDisabled</code
      > so keyboard focus stays on the button.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The banner is a <code>section</code>. Give it an <code>aria-label</code>
      so it is a named region that screen reader users can jump to. Put <code
        >role="status"</code
      > on a normal message and <code>role="alert"</code> on an error, so changes
      are announced. All actions are normal controls in tab order.
    </p>
    <p>
      If an action removes the banner, move focus to a sensible control, as the
      examples do. The banner fades in over 180ms and does not animate when
      reduced motion is requested. In forced colors mode the line uses the
      system text color.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      The background uses <code>--sprout-surface</code>, the line uses <code
        >--sprout-line</code
      >, and text uses <code>--sprout-muted</code>. A warning lead can use <code
        >--sprout-warning</code
      >. Motion uses <code>--sprout-motion-normal</code> and <code
        >--sprout-motion-ease</code
      >.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
